    "sentences": [
      {
        "text": "When a horsefly bites you, it presses six needle -like tools against your skin.",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 5.12,
        "words": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Two of them have sharp edges, so they slice you open like scissors, while two more have tiny teeth like a saw, sawing up and down to tear open your blood vessels until they burst and you start to bleed.",
        "start": 5.46,
        "end": 17.86,
        "words": 40
      },
      {
        "text": "Next, a hollow blade pumps in spit, which stops the cut from sealing so the blood keeps flowing out as its spongy tip laps it up.",
        "start": 18.18,
        "end": 27.04,
        "words": 26
      }
    ],
